  "family": "rock_punk",
  "lineage": "1990s heavy-metal subgenre developed from doom metal's extreme deceleration, characterized by extreme-down-tuned distorted-guitar drone textures, glacial tempi (often single notes sustained 30-90 seconds), heavy amplifier-and-feedback emphasis, and minimal-to-absent traditional rhythmic-or-vocal content. Earth's Earth 2 (1993, Dylan Carlson) inaugurated the canonical sound; Sunn O))) (Stephen O'Malley and Greg Anderson, founded 1998), Boris, and the broader Southern Lord Records label roster anchor the canonical drone metal aesthetic.",
